From: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: gate Proton 11 thread priority->nice mapping and
 main-thread boost

Proton 11 added a Windows-priority -> Linux-nice mapping in
apply_thread_priority() together with a +1 main-thread priority boost in
get_effective_thread_priority() (Valve commit 622da4759, "server: Boost
main thread priority").

For heavily multi-threaded async-streaming engines (Messiah / Where Winds
Meet) this over-prioritises a small set of producer/coordinator threads
(measured: ~10 game threads pulled from nice -5 to nice -8) relative to
the ~150 nice-0 job-worker threads. The workers get starved, the
producer/consumer pipeline runs out of phase, and the async loading
scheduler re-dispatches ~2-3x more completion cycles, stretching world
settle from ~15s (Proton 10) to ~50s.

Add two runtime gates so the behaviour can be disabled per game without a
rebuild:

  WINE_DISABLE_MAIN_THREAD_BOOST=1  drop only the +1 main-thread boost
  WINE_DISABLE_THREAD_NICE=1        disable the nice mapping entirely
                                    (flat nice 0, Proton-10 scheduling)

Both default off (unset) so no other title changes behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/server/thread.c b/server/thread.c
index 5c4a6bd0..391a7deb 100644
--- a/server/thread.c
+++ b/server/thread.c
@@ -260,7 +260,17 @@ void init_threading(void)
 static void apply_thread_priority( struct thread *thread )
 {
     int min = -nice_limit, max = nice_limit, range = max - min, niceness;
-    int effective_priority = get_effective_thread_priority( thread );
+    int effective_priority;
+    static int no_nice = -1;
+
+    if (no_nice < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "WINE_DISABLE_THREAD_NICE" );
+        no_nice = (e && atoi( e )) ? 1 : 0;
+    }
+    if (no_nice) return;
+
+    effective_priority = get_effective_thread_priority( thread );
 
     if (nice_limit >= 0) return;
 
@@ -857,11 +867,18 @@ affinity_t get_thread_affinity( struct thread *thread )
 int get_effective_thread_priority( struct thread *thread )
 {
     int priority = thread->priority;
+    static int no_boost = -1;
+
+    if (no_boost < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "WINE_DISABLE_MAIN_THREAD_BOOST" );
+        no_boost = (e && atoi( e )) ? 1 : 0;
+    }
 
     if (thread->disable_boost || priority >= LOW_REALTIME_PRIORITY)
         return priority;
 
-    if (get_process_first_thread( thread->process ) == thread)
+    if (!no_boost && get_process_first_thread( thread->process ) == thread)
         priority++;
 
     return min( priority, LOW_REALTIME_PRIORITY - 1 );
